//@version=6
// ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
// ║  BUILD STAMP — this file last CHANGED in v38   (F-A41 HTF trend; compile fix)║
// ║  Compare against the build record in chat. If they differ, the copy on your   ║
// ║  chart is STALE — re-paste. Stale scripts throw errors already fixed here:    ║
// ║  e.g. a pre-fix EdgeCases threw "Row 70 is out of table bounds" on a build    ║
// ║  whose table has had 100 rows since the first audited version.                ║
// ║  The stamp only moves when THIS file changes, so an unchanged file keeps its  ║
// ║  old number and still matches the record.                                     ║
// ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝
// A/B COST MODEL (pinned in code, NOT left to the Properties tab). Commission and
// slippage default to ZERO in TradingView, and zero costs systematically FLATTER the
// Treatment arm specifically: it is designed to fire materially more trades, so it pays
// more spread, and a costless test hides exactly the degradation the acceptance criteria
// are meant to measure. Pinning them here also removes the risk of the two arms being
// run under different Properties settings, which would invalidate the comparison
// outright. slippage is in TICKS; commission is cash per contract per side. TUNE BOTH
// to your own broker's XAUUSD fill quality before trusting absolute P&L — but keep them
// IDENTICAL across the two arms, which is what actually matters for a gate-only A/B.
//
// CHANGE ID: P0-CAL-002 — SELF-CORRECTION of the values pinned in the previous pass, and
// reconciliation of the TWO cost models that were silently disagreeing.
//   (1) UNIT ERROR (mine): strategy()'s `slippage` is denominated in TICKS, while the
//       Master's internal analog-cost model uses slippagePts in POINTS. `slippage=2` was
//       therefore 0.02 points/side at a 0.01 mintick — 10x too small (100x at 0.001) —
//       against the 0.2 points/side the expectancy engine assumes. Now 20 ticks = 0.20
//       points/side at mintick 0.01, matching slippagePts exactly.
//   (2) COMMISSION DIVERGENCE: commissionL defaulted to 0.0, so the Master's EV/veto
//       priced commission at ZERO while the backtest charged it. Both now assume the
//       same ~$7/lot round turn (commissionL=7.0; 3.50 per contract per SIDE here).
// WHY THIS MATTERS beyond tidiness: the Master's cost model feeds _costATR, which feeds
// analog expectancy, which drives the negative-expectancy VETO. Mispricing cost there
// means the system SELECTS trades under one cost assumption and is SCORED under another
// — an A/B measured on that basis is not measuring the gates. Selector and scorer must
// agree.
//
// CHANGE ID: P0-CAL-004 — values above DERIVED, not guessed, and proven equal by the
// cost-equivalence harness (cost_invariant.py). Two further faults this exposed:
//
//   (A) QTY UNIT ERROR (100x). strategy() qty is in UNITS OF THE BASE INSTRUMENT; for
//       spot XAUUSD the base is XAU = ONE TROY OUNCE, so qty=1 is 1 oz, NOT one 100oz
//       lot. commission_value=3.50 "per contract" therefore charged $3.50 per OUNCE per
//       side = $700 round turn per lot — 100x the intended $7/lot. Since pointValue=100
//       encodes 100 oz/lot, the correct figure is 7.00/100/2 = 0.035 per contract PER SIDE.
//
//   (B) THE ENGINE HAS NO SPREAD PARAMETER. The selector charges _sessSpread; the scorer
//       charged nothing for it. Spread is therefore FOLDED INTO slippage here. With the
//       spreadCost input at its 0.3 default, _sessSpread = max(floor, 0.3) collapses to
//       0.30 for killzone/NY/London alike, so one constant matches every in-session bar
//       exactly: (0.30 spread + 0.40 slip round trip) / 2 / 0.01 = 35 ticks.
//
// DERIVATION — recompute these if you change ANY of spreadCost, slippagePts, commissionL,
// pointValue or mintick, or the two models silently desynchronise again:
//   commission_value = commissionL / (pointValue) / 2
//   slippage_ticks   = (spreadCost + 2*slippagePts) / 2 / syminfo.mintick
//
// KNOWN RESIDUAL (accepted, documented): off-session bars carry a 0.50 spread floor in
// the selector vs the 0.30 folded in here — the scorer under-charges them by 0.20 points.
// strategy() takes ONE constant, so no single value can match a session-varying spread.
// The sessionQuality >= 30 hard gate excludes off-session bars in practice, so this
// residual should affect no trade the A/B actually takes; if you lower that gate, revisit.
//
// CHANGE ID: P0-CAL-006 (v15) — THE COST MODEL NO LONGER DEPENDS ON TICK SIZE.
//   strategy()'s `slippage` is a CONSTANT count of TICKS, so it could only be right for
//   one mintick: OANDA:XAUUSD quotes to 0.001, and the 35-tick constant would have charged
//   0.035 pts/side instead of 0.35 -- which is why the P0-CAL-005 gate blocked every entry.
//   The same cost is now charged as CASH per contract (1 contract = 1 oz, 1 pt = $1/oz):
//       commission_value = commissionL / pointValue / 2  +  (spreadCost + 2*slippagePts) / 2
//                        = 7 / 100 / 2 + (0.30 + 0.40) / 2 = 0.035 + 0.35 = 0.385 per side
//   and slippage = 0. P&L is identical for market fills at any tick size. KNOWN, ACCEPTED:
//   TradingView applies `slippage` to market/stop fills but not to LIMIT fills, whereas cash
//   commission applies to every fill -- so TP-limit exits are now charged up to 0.35 pts/oz
//   more than before. Conservative, and stated.
//   The gate now checks what this model actually depends on: 1 contract = $1 per point
//   (syminfo.pointvalue == 1) quoted in USD. Tick size no longer matters.
// These are BROKER-SPECIFIC, not universal truths. $7/lot round turn and 0.2 pts/side are
// mid-range retail ECN gold figures. Replace with your own fills, rerun the derivation
// above, and keep BOTH arms identical.
strategy("XAUUSD Quantum 5.0 — H2 Sweep-to-Value", overlay=true, max_lines_count=500, max_labels_count=500, max_boxes_count=500, max_bars_back=5000, initial_capital=10000, default_qty_type=strategy.fixed, default_qty_value=1, calc_on_every_tick=false, process_orders_on_close=true, commission_type=strategy.commission.cash_per_contract, commission_value=0.385, slippage=0)
// FILE ROLE: H2 ARM (v36, pre-registered in audit/PREREGISTRATION.md amendment A3) — FORWARD TEST
// ONLY. A self-contained strategy: the H2 sweep-to-value signal (the fenced H2 block,
// byte-identical to the one in Visuals) traded through the SAME execution layer, cost
// model and scorecard as the Treatment / Control / Challenger arms, so the four are comparable.
// It does not use the Quantum engine. Canonical live file = the Master.
// H2-TREND-BEGIN — per file. Visuals and Strategy_H2 request 1H / 4H / 1D themselves; the Master
// reads its engine's byte-identical requests instead (see the Master's H2-TREND block).
h2HtfScore(float _c, float _e20, float _e100, float _e200) => na(_c) ? 50.0 : (not na(_e200) and _c > _e200 ? 40.0 : 0.0) + (not na(_e20) and not na(_e100) and _e20 > _e100 ? 40.0 : 0.0) + (not na(_e20) and _c > _e20 ? 20.0 : 0.0)
// F-A41 (v38): every HIGHER-timeframe request.security in this file that asks for an offset value
// ([1] / [2]) now uses barmerge.lookahead_on. With lookahead_off, close[1] on a higher timeframe is
// TWO bars back on historical bars but ONE bar back live (measured on the operator's chart: daily
// close two days old on 6,027 of 6,091 bars), so backtest/record and live alerts saw different data.
// [1] + lookahead_on = the last COMPLETED higher-timeframe bar, identical live and in history; no
// lookahead, because every value is offset. Same-timeframe requests (timeframe.period) are unchanged.
[h2C1, h2A1, h2B1, h2D1] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "60", [close[1], ta.ema(close[1], 20), ta.ema(close[1], 100), ta.ema(close[1], 200)], barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_on)
[h2C4, h2A4, h2B4, h2D4] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "240", [close[1], ta.ema(close[1], 20), ta.ema(close[1], 100), ta.ema(close[1], 200)], barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_on)
[h2CD, h2AD, h2BD, h2DD] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", [close[1], ta.ema(close[1], 20), ta.ema(close[1], 100), ta.ema(close[1], 200)], barmerge.gaps_off, barmerge.lookahead_on)
float h2S1 = h2HtfScore(h2C1, h2A1, h2B1, h2D1)
float h2S4 = h2HtfScore(h2C4, h2A4, h2B4, h2D4)
float h2SD = h2HtfScore(h2CD, h2AD, h2BD, h2DD)
// H2-TREND-END
// H2-BEGIN
// ═══ HYPOTHESIS H2 — SWEEP-TO-VALUE (pre-registered: PREREGISTRATION amendment A3) ═══
// Operator's specification: a signal from the market trend, swing highs and lows, a liquidity
// sweep, the volume profile, and the next expected movement. This block is byte-identical in
// XAUUSD_Quantum_5_5_Visuals.pine (chart signals + H2 card) and XAUUSD_Quantum_5_0_Strategy_H2.pine
// (the forward-test arm); audit/tools/h2_parity.py fails otherwise.
// Every number is fixed in advance and borrowed from the existing system, not fitted:
//   trend  = the engine's HTF trend score on COMPLETED 1H / 4H / 1D bars (>= 60 up, <= 40 down),
//            at least 2 of the 3 agreeing
//   swings = 5-bar pivots (the Visuals structure default); a swing is liquidity until price
//            trades through it once, then it is consumed
//   sweep  = the confirmed bar trades through the last unconsumed swing low (high) and CLOSES
//            back above (below) it
//   value  = the engine's volume profile, rebuilt on every confirmed bar: 100 bars, 40 bins,
//            typical price, POC and a 70% value area (OANDA volume is tick volume; Diagnostics
//            reports its correlation with COMEX volume)
//   entry  = long only at or below the POC (discount), short only at or above it (premium)
//   plan   = stop beyond the sweep wick by 0.15 ATR (the engine's buffer), risk 0.5-5 ATR (the
//            engine's R bounds); TP1 = POC or 1R, TP2 = VAH (VAL) or 2R, whichever is farther
// Evaluated on confirmed bars only; reads nothing from the future.
int h2UpN = (h2S1 >= 60 ? 1 : 0) + (h2S4 >= 60 ? 1 : 0) + (h2SD >= 60 ? 1 : 0)
int h2DnN = (h2S1 <= 40 ? 1 : 0) + (h2S4 <= 40 ? 1 : 0) + (h2SD <= 40 ? 1 : 0)
bool h2TrendUp = h2UpN >= 2
bool h2TrendDn = h2DnN >= 2
// swings: the last unconsumed 5-bar pivot on each side
float h2PH = ta.pivothigh(high, 5, 5)
float h2PL = ta.pivotlow(low, 5, 5)
var float h2SwH = na
var float h2SwL = na
bool h2SweepL = barstate.isconfirmed and not na(h2SwL) and low < h2SwL and close > h2SwL
bool h2SweepH = barstate.isconfirmed and not na(h2SwH) and high > h2SwH and close < h2SwH
float h2SweptLvl = h2SweepL ? h2SwL : h2SweepH ? h2SwH : na
if barstate.isconfirmed and not na(h2SwL) and low < h2SwL
    h2SwL := na
if barstate.isconfirmed and not na(h2SwH) and high > h2SwH
    h2SwH := na
if not na(h2PL)
    h2SwL := h2PL
if not na(h2PH)
    h2SwH := h2PH
// volume profile, rebuilt on every confirmed bar (the engine's definition)
float h2VHi = ta.highest(high, 100)
float h2VLo = ta.lowest(low, 100)
var float h2Poc = na
var float h2Vah = na
var float h2Val = na
if barstate.isconfirmed and bar_index >= 100 and h2VHi > h2VLo
    float _h2bs = (h2VHi - h2VLo) / 40.0
    float[] _h2vv = array.new_float(40, 0.0)
    for _h2i = 0 to 99
        int _h2k = math.max(0, math.min(int(((high[_h2i] + low[_h2i] + close[_h2i]) / 3.0 - h2VLo) / _h2bs), 39))
        array.set(_h2vv, _h2k, array.get(_h2vv, _h2k) + nz(volume[_h2i], 0.0))
    float _h2mx = 0.0
    int _h2pk = 0
    for _h2j = 0 to 39
        if array.get(_h2vv, _h2j) > _h2mx
            _h2mx := array.get(_h2vv, _h2j)
            _h2pk := _h2j
    float _h2cum = _h2mx
    float _h2tgt = array.sum(_h2vv) * 0.70
    int _h2lo = _h2pk
    int _h2hi = _h2pk
    while _h2cum < _h2tgt and (_h2lo > 0 or _h2hi < 39)
        float _h2vb = _h2lo > 0 ? array.get(_h2vv, _h2lo - 1) : -1.0
        float _h2va = _h2hi < 39 ? array.get(_h2vv, _h2hi + 1) : -1.0
        if _h2va >= _h2vb and _h2hi < 39
            _h2hi += 1
            _h2cum += _h2va
        else if _h2lo > 0
            _h2lo -= 1
            _h2cum += _h2vb
        else
            break
    h2Poc := h2VLo + _h2bs * (_h2pk + 0.5)
    h2Vah := h2VLo + _h2bs * (_h2hi + 0.5)
    h2Val := h2VLo + _h2bs * (_h2lo + 0.5)
// the signal and its plan
float h2Atr = ta.atr(14)
float h2RL = h2SweepL ? close - (low - 0.15 * h2Atr) : na
float h2RS = h2SweepH ? (high + 0.15 * h2Atr) - close : na
bool h2Long = h2SweepL and h2TrendUp and not na(h2Poc) and close <= h2Poc and h2RL >= 0.5 * h2Atr and h2RL <= 5.0 * h2Atr
bool h2Short = h2SweepH and h2TrendDn and not na(h2Poc) and close >= h2Poc and h2RS >= 0.5 * h2Atr and h2RS <= 5.0 * h2Atr
float h2R = h2Long ? h2RL : h2Short ? h2RS : na
float h2Sl = h2Long ? close - h2RL : h2Short ? close + h2RS : na
float h2Tp1 = h2Long ? math.max(h2Poc, close + h2R) : h2Short ? math.min(h2Poc, close - h2R) : na
float h2Tp2 = h2Long ? math.max(h2Vah, close + 2.0 * h2R) : h2Short ? math.min(h2Val, close - 2.0 * h2R) : na
// H2-END

bool _costModelValid = syminfo.pointvalue == 1.0 and syminfo.currency == "USD"
var label _mtWarn = na
if barstate.islast and not _costModelValid
    label.delete(_mtWarn)
    _mtWarn := label.new(bar_index, high, "A/B INVALID — COST MODEL MISMATCH\npointvalue=" + str.tostring(syminfo.pointvalue) + " currency=" + syminfo.currency + "\n(cash costs derived for 1 contract = $1/pt, USD)\nENTRIES BLOCKED until corrected", color=color.new(color.red, 0), textcolor=color.white, style=label.style_label_down, size=size.large)

float abTestQty = 1.0
// Q5.6: entries additionally blocked by the account-state risk lockout, so the twin
// backtests EXACTLY what the indicator recommends (tqVeto already folds in riskLock).
// P0-CAL-005: `and _costModelValid` is the HARD GATE. On a feed whose tick size the
// declared cost constants were not derived for, the twin takes NO trades at all, so the
// Strategy Tester reports a visibly empty run instead of a plausible but invalid one.
bool execBuyS = h2Long and _costModelValid
bool execSellS = h2Short and _costModelValid
var float stEntry = na
var float stSL = na
var float stTP1 = na
var float stTP2 = na
var bool stBE = false
if execBuyS and strategy.position_size <= 0
    strategy.close_all(comment="flip")
    stEntry := close
    stSL := h2Sl
    stTP1 := h2Tp1
    stTP2 := h2Tp2
    stBE := false
    // P0-EXEC-001 (external audit): qty is now EXPLICIT. Previously omitted, so the
    // order fell through to default_qty_type=percent_of_equity/5 — i.e. 5% of equity
    // notional, which is neither the dashboard's risk-based lot nor a constant size.
    // Worse for an A/B: percent_of_equity COMPOUNDS, so the two arms would trade
    // different sizes as their equity curves diverged, contaminating the very
    // comparison the twins exist to make. Fixed size makes trade outcomes additive in
    // R and the gate change the only variable. Absolute P&L is therefore NOT a
    // risk-model simulation — it is a like-for-like gate comparison, which is the
    // twins' only purpose.
    // CHANGE ID: F-013 — stamp the engine's own per-trade estimates into the entry
    // COMMENT, which TradingView writes to the Signal column of the List of Trades
    // export. This is METADATA ONLY: comment has zero effect on fills, sizing, or any
    // result. It is applied to BOTH arms so the A/B delta is unchanged.
    // WHY IT MUST PRECEDE THE BASELINE: validate.py's calibration test needs a `prob`
    // and `tq` per trade, and those are internal engine values absent from the standard
    // export. alert() CANNOT supply them — alerts fire only forward in real time and
    // never on historical bars, so they can never backfill a backtest. The entry comment
    // is the only mechanism that attaches them to every historical trade. Without this,
    // the baseline export cannot support the calibration test and a second full run
    // F-A12 FIX. That format was NEVER EMITTED: the comment shipped TQ|CG|B..V..|D and
    // carried no probability at all, so the one field the calibration test actually needs
    // was the one field missing -- and the defect hid behind a comment describing the
    // intended format rather than the real one. P is now appended, and it is the
    // DIRECTIONAL probability: _calibratedProb for longs, 1 - _calibratedProb for shorts,
    // i.e. P(this trade wins) rather than P(bullish). A reliability curve needs the
    // former. Emitted format is now "TQ<n>|CG<n>|B<n>V<n>|D<n>|P<pct>".
    // This had to land BEFORE the baseline run for the reason stated just above: alerts
    // cannot backfill history, so without it the export cannot support the calibration
    // test and a second full backtest would be needed to get it.
    strategy.entry("L", strategy.long, qty = abTestQty, comment = "H2 R" + str.tostring(h2R, "#.##"))
if execSellS and strategy.position_size >= 0
    strategy.close_all(comment="flip")
    stEntry := close
    stSL := h2Sl
    stTP1 := h2Tp1
    stTP2 := h2Tp2
    stBE := false
    strategy.entry("S", strategy.short, qty = abTestQty, comment = "H2 R" + str.tostring(h2R, "#.##"))
// CHANGE ID: P0-EXEC-002-FIX | FILE: Strategy execution layer (both twins)
// OLD LOGIC: on the bar where high>=stTP1, stSL was mutated to breakeven BEFORE
// being passed to strategy.exit() the SAME bar, with no check for whether the
// ORIGINAL stop was also touched this bar. TradingView cannot determine intrabar
// touch order from OHLC alone (documented limitation, not fixable by
// calc_on_every_tick) — so a bar whose low breached the original stop AND whose
// high reached TP1 was silently resolved as "TP1 then breakeven," which is
// optimistic if the stop was actually touched first.
// NEW LOGIC: only move to breakeven if TP1 was touched AND the ORIGINAL stop was
// NOT also touched this same bar. If both were touched, stSL is left unmutated
// (original stop stays live) — this matches the stop-first convention already
// used elsewhere in this codebase (Q5.6 risk tracker: "SL assumed first if both
// hit in one bar"), applied here for consistency rather than invented fresh.
// EXPECTED EFFECT: fewer/later breakeven transitions on bars with a same-bar
// stop/TP1 conflict; no change on bars where only one level was touched.
// REGRESSION TESTS: (A) TP1 only, no stop touch -> BE as before. (B) stop only ->
// unaffected (existing branch). (C) both touched same bar -> stop wins, no BE.
if strategy.position_size > 0
    bool _slTouchedL = low <= stSL
    if not stBE and high >= stTP1 and not _slTouchedL
        stBE := true
        stSL := stEntry
    strategy.exit("Lx1", "L", stop=stSL, limit=stTP1, qty_percent=50)
    strategy.exit("Lx2", "L", stop=stSL, limit=stTP2)
if strategy.position_size < 0
    bool _slTouchedS = high >= stSL
    if not stBE and low <= stTP1 and not _slTouchedS
        stBE := true
        stSL := stEntry
    strategy.exit("Sx1", "S", stop=stSL, limit=stTP1, qty_percent=50)
    strategy.exit("Sx2", "S", stop=stSL, limit=stTP2)

// ═══ v34 FORWARD-TEST SCORECARD (display only: reads strategy.closedtrades, feeds nothing) ═══
// The record of THIS arm, inside TradingView. One row per POSITION: the 50% TP1 exit and the
// remainder are summed per entry, so a position closed in two parts counts once (the Strategy
// Tester's List of Trades shows each part as its own row). A position still partly open is left
// out until it closes. Rule (PREREGISTRATION §4): N >= 50, the 95% t-interval of the mean $ per
// position entirely above 0, and PF >= 1.2 -> EDGE SHOWN; below 50 -> COLLECTING. TradingView keeps
// nothing between sessions: the card is recomputed from the LOADED bars, so it is only as deep as
// the chart's history -- the Coverage row says when the history no longer reaches the start.
// v38 COMPILE FIX (operator's chart, 2026-10-05): input.time() needs a const int default, and
// timestamp("UTC", ...) returns a simple int (CE10123). 1791244800000 = 2026-10-06 00:00 UTC in ms (start moved by A5, F-A41).
fwdStart = input.time(1791244800000, "Forward test start (PREREGISTRATION A5)", group="FORWARD TEST")
fwdShow = input.bool(true, "Show forward-test scorecard", group="FORWARD TEST")
fwdPos = input.string("Bottom Right", "Scorecard position", options=["Bottom Right", "Bottom Left", "Top Right", "Top Left"], group="FORWARD TEST", tooltip="With several arms visible on one chart, give each its own corner.")
var int fwdBar0 = time
var table fwdTbl = table.new(fwdPos == "Bottom Left" ? position.bottom_left : fwdPos == "Top Right" ? position.top_right : fwdPos == "Top Left" ? position.top_left : position.bottom_right, 2, 9, bgcolor=color.new(#0B0F14, 5), border_width=1, border_color=color.new(#2A3340, 0))
_fwRow(int _r, string _k, string _fwv, color _c) =>
    table.cell(fwdTbl, 0, _r, _k, text_color=color.new(#8FA3B8, 0), text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_left)
    table.cell(fwdTbl, 1, _r, _fwv, text_color=_c, text_size=size.small, text_halign=text.align_left)
if fwdShow and barstate.islast
    int _fwct = strategy.closedtrades
    int _fwopenBar = strategy.opentrades > 0 ? strategy.opentrades.entry_bar_index(0) : -3
    int _fwn = 0
    int _fww = 0
    float _fws = 0.0
    float _fws2 = 0.0
    float _fwgw = 0.0
    float _fwgl = 0.0
    float _fwpos = 0.0
    int _fweb = -1
    int _fwfirst = 0
    for _fwi = 0 to _fwct
        int _fwb = -2
        bool _fwin = false
        if _fwi < _fwct
            _fwb := strategy.closedtrades.entry_bar_index(_fwi)
            _fwin := strategy.closedtrades.entry_time(_fwi) >= fwdStart
        if _fweb >= 0 and _fwb != _fweb and _fweb != _fwopenBar
            _fwn += 1
            _fww += _fwpos > 0 ? 1 : 0
            _fws += _fwpos
            _fws2 += _fwpos * _fwpos
            _fwgw += math.max(_fwpos, 0.0)
            _fwgl += math.max(-_fwpos, 0.0)
        if _fwb != _fweb
            _fwpos := 0.0
            _fweb := -1
        if _fwin
            _fweb := _fwb
            _fwpos += strategy.closedtrades.profit(_fwi)
            _fwfirst := _fwfirst == 0 ? strategy.closedtrades.entry_time(_fwi) : _fwfirst
    float _fwm = _fwn > 0 ? _fws / _fwn : na
    float _fwsd = _fwn > 1 ? math.sqrt(math.max((_fws2 - _fwn * _fwm * _fwm) / (_fwn - 1), 0.0)) : na
    // two-sided 95% t quantile by the Fisher expansion in z = 1.96 (error < 0.003 for df >= 10)
    float _fwdf = math.max(_fwn - 1, 1)
    float _fwt = 1.959964 + (7.529121 + 1.959964) / (4.0 * _fwdf) + (5.0 * 28.922809 + 16.0 * 7.529121 + 3.0 * 1.959964) / (96.0 * _fwdf * _fwdf)
    float _fwlo = _fwn >= 10 ? _fwm - _fwt * _fwsd / math.sqrt(_fwn) : na
    float _fwhi = _fwn >= 10 ? _fwm + _fwt * _fwsd / math.sqrt(_fwn) : na
    float _fwpf = _fwgl > 0 ? _fwgw / _fwgl : na
    // no losing position at all: PF is infinite, which passes the >= 1.2 rule (it is na above)
    bool _fwpfOk = _fwgl > 0 ? _fwpf >= 1.2 : _fwgw > 0
    string _fwv = _fwn < 50 ? "COLLECTING " + str.tostring(_fwn) + "/50" : _fwlo > 0 and _fwpfOk ? "EDGE SHOWN" : "NOT SHOWN"
    bool _fwtfOk = timeframe.in_seconds() == 900
    color _fwcT = color.new(#E6EDF3, 0)
    table.cell(fwdTbl, 0, 0, "FORWARD TEST  v35", text_color=color.white, bgcolor=color.new(#1F3A5F, 0), text_size=size.small)
    table.cell(fwdTbl, 1, 0, "from " + str.format_time(fwdStart, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm", "UTC") + " UTC  ·  " + timeframe.period + (_fwtfOk ? " (registered)" : "  NOT 15M: does not count"), text_color=_fwtfOk ? color.white : color.orange, bgcolor=color.new(#1F3A5F, 0), text_size=size.small)
    _fwRow(1, "Positions (N)", str.tostring(_fwn) + (_fwn > 0 ? "   wins " + str.tostring(_fww) + " = " + str.tostring(_fww * 100.0 / _fwn, "#") + "%" : ""), _fwcT)
    _fwRow(2, "Mean $ / position", na(_fwm) ? "—" : str.tostring(_fwm, "#.##"), _fwcT)
    _fwRow(3, "95% CI of mean", na(_fwlo) ? "needs 10+ positions" : str.tostring(_fwlo, "#.##") + "  to  " + str.tostring(_fwhi, "#.##"), _fwcT)
    _fwRow(4, "Profit factor", na(_fwpf) ? (_fwgw > 0 ? "no losses yet (infinite)" : "—") : str.tostring(_fwpf, "#.##") + "  (rule >= 1.2)", _fwcT)
    _fwRow(5, "Net $ (1 oz, pinned costs)", str.tostring(_fws, "#.##"), _fwcT)
    _fwRow(6, "VERDICT (pre-registered)", _fwv, _fwv == "EDGE SHOWN" ? color.lime : _fwv == "NOT SHOWN" ? color.orange : _fwcT)
    _fwRow(7, "Coverage", fwdBar0 > fwdStart ? "loaded history starts " + str.format_time(fwdBar0, "yyyy-MM-dd", "UTC") + " AFTER the test start: incomplete, use the weekly log" : _fwn == 0 ? "no closed position since the start yet" : "first counted entry " + str.format_time(_fwfirst, "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm", "UTC"), fwdBar0 > fwdStart ? color.orange : _fwcT)
    _fwRow(8, "Unit", "positions (partial exits summed); open positions excluded", color.new(#8FA3B8, 0))
